Falsifies `machine_discovery::x86_64::verification::a_feature_is_never_reported_from_a_leaf_the_part_does_not_answer`.

The defect: an *extended* leaf is gated on the *standard* maximum.

`CpuidWords` carries two maxima, `leaf0[0]` for the standard leaf space and
`extended_max_leaf` for the `0x8000_0000`-based one, and a part can answer every
standard leaf while implementing no extended leaf at all. This patch reads
`CPUID.80000001H:EDX` whenever the part answers standard leaf 1, which every
part made since 1993 does, so NX and SYSCALL are believed on the strength of a
maximum from the wrong space.

What that costs is not a wrong boot line. NX is what page-table `W^X` is made of
and SYSCALL is the whole ring-3 entry path, so milestone 524 (the three x86_64
boot gates) refuses a part reporting neither. With this patch the refusal is
computed from whatever `CPUID` returned for a leaf the part does not implement,
which on x86 is some other leaf's data rather than zero. The defect is invisible
on every machine this project owns, because they all answer the extended leaves,
which is exactly why the claim is proved over symbolic words instead of captured
ones.

Expected to fail: `assert!(!isa.features.contains(NX))`, under the
`w.extended_max_leaf < 0x8000_0001` branch, for words where `leaf0[0] >= 1` and
bit 20 of `extended_leaf1_edx` is set. `assert!(isa.missing_requirements().any())`
two lines below it fails on the same counterexample.

diff --git a/crates/machine_discovery/src/x86_64.rs b/crates/machine_discovery/src/x86_64.rs
index f21de9f20..ce4118889 100644
--- a/crates/machine_discovery/src/x86_64.rs
+++ b/crates/machine_discovery/src/x86_64.rs
@@ -963,7 +963,7 @@ impl Isa {
         }
 
         let mut features = Features::NONE;
-        if w.extended_max_leaf >= 0x8000_0001 {
+        if w.leaf0[0] >= 1 {
             if w.extended_leaf1_edx & (1 << 20) != 0 {
                 features = features.union(NX);
             }
